&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover is an award-winning communications consultancy that advises enterprises, institutions, and individuals on building recognition and enhancing reputation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;From our offices across Europe and the Middle East, we adopt an integrated approach that connects the dots across channels, audiences and issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our collective of smart, curious people think differently and live by a shared mission, purpose, vision, and values. These shape how we work, not just with our colleagues, but with clients and partners too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to ‘rewire communications for impact’ and harness its transformative power to advocate, trailblaze and make a difference.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We do this by igniting and empowering the potential of every individual within our company, recognising that each person is a unique spark, capable of creating extraordinary impact. We believe that by nurturing and harnessing the collective brilliance of our people, we can drive innovation, foster an uncommon work culture, and make a positive difference to society.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Embracing the complete range of skills and services across the communications spectrum without constraint, we create the best outcomes for our clients and deliver world-class work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and skilled Account Executive to join our Healthcare Communications team, joining a team of experts in product PR, patient advocacy, crisis management, disease awareness, corporate communications and media relations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Account Executive provides high-quality public relations services to Hanover’s existing healthcare clients, together with timely research and administrative support for new business activity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Account Executive is also responsible for supporting media outreach, providing administrative support for client meetings, and establishing demonstrably credible working relationships with clients, where appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay abreast of the media, with the goal of identifying opportunities for coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft high quality materials for client review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain relevant records of target stakeholder and audience groups relevant to your clients and sectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver specifically assigned areas of each discrete/new project to agreed timescales, on budget and to a high quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct value-add research and produce high quality draft intelligence reports for existing clients and sector specific new business meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft client meeting agendas and effective action notes arising from internal account meetings and sector specific new business meetings, together with efficient maintenance of new business databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute towards selected new business pitches as part of the wider team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a relevant PR and communications position from either a public relations consultancy or in-house communications team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good knowledge and understanding of healthcare communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communications skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and highly organised&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective time management and strong organisational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of working collaboratively as part of a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable interest in media, news and current affairs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, your core benefits package will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus potential linked to recruitment, new business and long service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days’ annual leave (plus bank holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private healthcare and dental insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company pension plan, including 5% employer contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also have access to a wide range of opportunities and initiatives, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working policies, plus eligibility to apply for a sabbatical after 2 years’ service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Summer Fridays finish (3pm) – early Friday finish the rest of the year (4pm)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Hanover Academy, which incorporates training, coaching, mentoring and reverse-mentoring opportunities to support personal development and career progression across all levels, with a generous training budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International secondments as well as the opportunity to collaborate with all offices across the AVENIR GLOBAL’s network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A wellbeing programme, featuring (but not limited to) pre- and post-maternity leave coaching, a working parents’ group, subsidised gym membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our Culture Club, with a robust social calendar all year round and CSR activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Statement +&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover Communications is an equal opportunities employer, committed to creating and ensuring a fair, inclusive, and diverse work environment where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity. We believe that equality and diversity are essential to high performance and a thriving culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We maintain a strict no-tolerance stance against any form of discrimination and harassment, ensuring all individuals are treated equitably, irrespective of their race, ethnicity, religion, beliefs, age, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, marital or pregnancy status, genetic background, or any other attribute safeguarded under our company policies or federal, state or local laws and legislation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to ensure that our hiring process is accessible. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application process, please send an email to &lt;a ---------- with the nature of your request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to transparency about how we collect and use your data, including ensuring we comply with legal obligations relating to data protection. You can view our data privacy policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://hanovercomms.com/recruitment-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover is part of AVENIR GLOBAL’s powerhouse of specialist communications consultancies across EMEA and North America. Collectively we rank among the top 15 largest communication firms in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hanovercomms.com/about-us/&quot;&gt;Hanover&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hanovercomms.com/careers/&quot;&gt;working for us&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover is an award-winning communications consultancy that advises enterprises, institutions, and individuals on building recognition and enhancing reputation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;From our offices across Europe and the Middle East, we adopt an integrated approach that connects the dots across channels, audiences and issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our collective of smart, curious people think differently and live by a shared mission, purpose, vision, and values. These shape how we work, not just with our colleagues, but with clients and partners too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to ‘rewire communications for impact’ and harness its transformative power to advocate, trailblaze and make a difference.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We do this by igniting and empowering the potential of every individual within our company, recognising that each person is a unique spark, capable of creating extraordinary impact. We believe that by nurturing and harnessing the collective brilliance of our people, we can drive innovation, foster an uncommon work culture, and make a positive difference to society.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Embracing the complete range of skills and services across the communications spectrum without constraint, we create the best outcomes for our clients and deliver world-class work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hanover is actively seeking a highly experienced and dynamic Account Director to become an integral part of our Healthcare Policy, Advocacy &amp;amp; Public Affairs team. This is an exceptional opportunity for someone to leverage their expertise in the healthcare sector and make a significant impact on our client services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Director, you will lead client relationships, providing senior strategic counsel and ensuring delivery of high-quality, commercially successful account programmes. You will guide clients through the complex landscape of healthcare policy, advocacy, and public affairs, while leading account teams and overseeing programme delivery and budgets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will play a leading role in new business activity, including acquisition, development and pitching, alongside managing and mentoring junior team members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will be based in London and offers the opportunity to work across clients we share with our offices in Brussels, Dublin and the Middle East, as well as integrated accounts with our Healthcare Communications and Digital teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team works across a range of services including government relations, public affairs, market access, policy, advocacy and corporate communications across health and business. With over half of the world’s top 20 pharmaceutical companies, as well as NHS providers, health technology businesses and charities amongst our clients, we offer a diverse and compelling range of issues and opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead client accounts, ensuring high-quality delivery, strong client satisfaction and commercial performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead high-impact political and NHS campaigns to deliver tangible policy change for our clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-profile events and stakeholder engagement programmes involving politicians, policymakers, NHS stakeholders and patient groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver high-quality strategic intelligence and insights to our clients by utilising the Hanover network and building your own network and expertise across policy areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an uncompromising commitment to detail, rigorously reviewing all communications, reports and client deliverables to ensure accuracy and professionalism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to grow existing client relationships and broaden Hanover’s offer across accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement innovative strategies for growth, staying ahead of industry trends and positioning Hanover as a leader in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a lead on new business pitches, being a core part of the team in building creative strategies and tactics and pitching to clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver marketing activity to support Hanover Health’s business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the management of expert steering groups to drive thought-leadership for our clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal management of junior members of the team providing guidance on professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active participant in championing the mission, vision, purpose, values and behaviours of Hanover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognise and value the diverse backgrounds, skills, and perspectives of all individuals at Hanover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant experience from a public affairs consultancy, in-house public affairs department, patient group/NGO, Parliament, or other relevant organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent knowledge of health policy and ability to analyse developments within the NHS and commercial environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of success in account management within the healthcare policy, advocacy, or public affairs sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eye for detail and ability to think critically about your own work and that of others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional leadership skills with the ability to inspire and guide teams towards achieving shared goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen with experience in managing budgets and driving business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic judgement and ability to provide credible counsel to senior clients in complex and fast-moving policy environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, capable of building rapport with clients, team members, and stakeholders at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to professional development, both for self-improvement and for the mentorship of junior colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, your core benefits package will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus potential linked to recruitment, new business and long service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days’ annual leave (plus bank holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private healthcare and dental insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company pension plan, including 5% employer contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also have access to a wide range of opportunities and initiatives, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working policies, plus eligibility to apply for a sabbatical after 2 years’ service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Summer Fridays finish (3pm) – early Friday finish the rest of the year (4pm)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Hanover Academy, which incorporates training, coaching, mentoring and reverse-mentoring opportunities to support personal development and career progression across all levels, with a generous training budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International secondments as well as the opportunity to collaborate with all offices across the AVENIR GLOBAL’s network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A wellbeing programme, featuring (but not limited to) pre- and post-maternity leave coaching, a working parents’ group, subsidised gym membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our Culture Club, with a robust social calendar all year round and CSR activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Statement +&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover Communications is an equal opportunities employer, committed to creating and ensuring a fair, inclusive, and diverse work environment where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity. We believe that equality and diversity are essential to high performance and a thriving culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We maintain a strict no-tolerance stance against any form of discrimination and harassment, ensuring all individuals are treated equitably, irrespective of their race, ethnicity, religion, beliefs, age, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, marital or pregnancy status, genetic background, or any other attribute safeguarded under our company policies or federal, state or local laws and legislation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to ensure that our hiring process is accessible. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application process, please send an email to &lt;a ---------- with the nature of your request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to transparency about how we collect and use your data, including ensuring we comply with legal obligations relating to data protection. You can view our data privacy policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://hanovercomms.com/recruitment-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover is part of AVENIR GLOBAL’s powerhouse of specialist communications consultancies across EMEA and North America. Collectively we rank among the top 15 largest communication firms in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hanovercomms.com/about-us/&quot;&gt;Hanover&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hanovercomms.com/careers/&quot;&gt;working for us&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Type: &lt;/strong&gt;Full-time, salaried employment&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote, United Kingdom only.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range: &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;£90,000 - £105,000 + stock options.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Focal Systems is the industry leader in retail AI solutions. We are headquartered in San Francisco, California with operations in Canada and the UK, and a tech-hub in Poland. We are a Deep Learning first company. Our mission is to automate and optimize brick and mortar retail using deep learning computer vision. Focal Systems has been deployed at scale with some of the top retailers in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek smart, creative and passionate people who want to help build a great and enduring company and deploy Deep Learning to the world!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Responsible For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Product Manager, you will take ownership of how data is processed at Focal, and shape what that path becomes: from the imports that bring a retailer&#39;s planograms, inventory and store metadata into our platform, through the pipelines that turn them into signal, to the metrics and reports their head office acts on. You will work with data engineering, data scientists, analytics, customer success and the retailers themselves. What you build are data products, and the measure of one is what a retailer does differently because of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role. You will set direction and priorities as we roll out to hundreds of new stores, but you are also expected to know the systems well enough to be a partner in an engineering design conversation, pull your own numbers when something looks wrong, and hold a strong position in the discussions with customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a peer to the engineers you work with, someone who understands the systems well enough to know what is expensive and why and when to push back&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are drawn to the seams between teams, where ownership is shared and the hardest problems live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write your own queries and interrogate the answers before anyone else has to, and you can name the business number a data product of yours moved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can change your mind in a technical argument, and you can point to the time you did&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong judgment about what not to build, and you have killed your own work when it stopped earning its place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use AI as part of how you actually work, and you have built things with it that other people went on to use, not demos you gave once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate complicated things crisply to people who do not share your context, including customers hearing an answer they did not want&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build things that outlast you, whether runbooks, tooling or documented decisions, because you would rather remove yourself as a dependency than be indispensable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own product direction for the full data path, from how a retailer&#39;s data arrives to what our reports say, and set the priorities where the two ends pull against each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own how customer data gets into Focal: imports, planograms, store metadata, cut-off configuration, and the chain-specific flows each retailer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own what comes out and whether anyone acts on it: the metrics, the reporting APIs, the insight-generating agents, and the customer-facing dashboards a head office runs its week on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run discovery with retailers and store colleagues, and turn what you learn into a product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship, then find out whether anyone used it, and act on the answer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate your own work with AI and share what you build with the rest of the product team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Need to Be Successful&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in product management, including real time on a technically deep product where you owned integrations, data, or both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough technical depth to reason about APIs, data pipelines and system boundaries, and to be an equal partner in an engineering discussion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building for a hierarchy of users who need different things from the same data: a store manager, a regional director and a head of supply chain reading one dataset three ways, served by one configurable surface&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on comfort with SQL and the ability to answer your own data questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in the analytics and BI tooling landscape, and a view on what makes a dashboard worth returning to rather than merely correct&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of a product roadmap end to end, from problem definition through to something shipped and adopted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of getting things done across teams, and the communication to influence engineering and commercial partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with enterprise customers, including holding a position they disagree with&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating remote-first, across a distributed team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel occasionally for store and customer visits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Would Set You Apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working with high-volume, noisy sensor or computer-vision data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with change data capture into a cloud warehouse (ideally Snowflake)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping AI-powered features, including the call on when a model is good enough to ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Focal Systems&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Focal Systems means becoming part of a company that&#39;s truly making a difference in the retail world. Here&#39;s why you should consider us:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Values and Mission: &lt;/strong&gt;We are a tightly-knit team with an ambitious mission and a strong set of core values, which define our approach to business and have successfully guided us since inception.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional Team: &lt;/strong&gt;We are a team of hard-working, fun-loving professionals from some of the most eminent universities, research labs, and tech companies of our time. We pride ourselves on recruiting exceptional individuals to help us redefine the state-of-the-art.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outstanding Partners:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;We work with 10+ of the largest retailers in the world and have a world-class roster of investors, advisors and partners to support &amp;amp; advise us in our endeavours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care deeply about the health, happiness, and wellbeing of all of our employees. We offer:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Attractive Stock&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and Development Budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Clarity Innovations is a trusted national security partner, dedicated to safeguarding our nation’s interests and delivering innovative solutions that empower the Intelligence Community (IC) and Department of Defense (DoD) to transform data into actionable intelligence, ensuring mission success in an evolving world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission-first software and data engineering platform modernizes data operations, utilizing advanced workflows, CI/CD, and secure DevSecOps practices. We focus on challenges in Information Warfare, Cyber Operations, Operational Security, and Data Structuring, enabling end-to-end solutions that drive operational impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to delivering cutting-edge tools and capabilities that address the most complex national security challenges, empowering our partners to stay ahead of emerging threats and ensuring the success of their critical missions. At Clarity, we are people-focused and set on being a destination employer for top talent, offering an environment where innovation thrives, careers grow, and individuals are valued. Join us as we continue to lead innovation and tackle the most pressing challenges in national security.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;div&gt;This role is for a Data Scientist on a close-knit team supporting Air Force Special Operations Command (AFSOC) at RAF Mildenhall, UK. This team is at the center of helping the command empower and leverage its data for more effective analysis and decision making. As a subject matter expert, the Data Scientist will leverage their experience to gather and derive insights from complex data, assist the command with development initiatives, and facilitate digital transformation efforts. The work done in this role has a direct impact on mission readiness as the team&#39;s efforts go toward making a more resilient and data-driven organization.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Data Scientist will have skills sets of both data analysts and data engineers. Data scientists are responsible for designing, implementing, and maintaining a data pipeline. &amp;nbsp;In addition, data scientists shall interpret and analyze complex sets of data, as well as plan, execute, and manage ML projects with cloud-native platforms and advanced ML solutions. They understand some of the most challenging processes, technologies, and can leverage a vast array of methodologies in the field, such as data mining, natural language programming, and machine learning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data scientists must have a combination of skills that includes programming, mathematical modeling, statistics, and domain knowledge. They must combine an advanced math and statistics background with programming, domain knowledge, and communication skills to analyze data, create applied mathematical models, and present results in a form useful to the organization. &amp;nbsp;They must also be able to understand and manipulate structured and unstructured large data sets, which requires proficiency in distributed SQL programming, relational and non-relational data queries, general programming languages (such as Python and R,) and machine learning techniques.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Data Scientist shall perform the following tasks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Interpret and analyze data using exploratory mathematic and statistical techniques based on the scientific method.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Coordinate research and analytic activities utilizing various data points (unstructured and structured) and employ programming to clean, massage, and organize the data&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experiment against data points, provide information based on experiment results and provide previously undiscovered solutions to command data challenges.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Coordinate with Data Engineers to build Data environments providing data identified by other data professionals&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Apply and develop scientific methodology, statistics, and algorithms to discover and frame relevant problems, hypotheses, and opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Develop predictive and prescriptive modeling, natural language processing (NLP), Robotic Process Automation (RPA), text mining and processing, clustering, forecasting methods, and other advanced statistical techniques.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Design and automate processes to facilitate the manipulation and analysis of data. Manage and integrate data across dissimilar data sets. Analyze large-scale structured and unstructured data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Use frameworks such as Spark and Hadoop to conduct large-scale data processing. Perform statistical modeling and create data visualizations using products like Tableau, Microsoft Power BI and R Shiny.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Research, design, and implement algorithms to solve complex problems. Program using R, Python (NumPy, SciPy, Pandas) or similar analytical languages.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Perform data engineering, data processing and modeling techniques using cloud-based data management, data science, and ML platforms such as Databricks, IBM Cloud Pak, Cloudera, and Snowflake.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Communicate complex concepts and hypothesis to a non-technical audience through digital storytelling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 1 year of hands-on Data Science experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in a STEM field is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with one or more programming languages (Java, C++, Python, R, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to apply data science to solve real-world problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secret Clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with DoD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in Operations Research, Industrial Engineering, Applied Mathematics, Statistics, Physics, Computer Science, or related fields.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Envision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top Secret clearance with SCI eligibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary Range: $97,000 - $233,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;c-message_kit__gutter&quot;&gt;
